A mailbox's ring, through which a device receives from it, goes once no
running region, nor the GPU process whose mailbox it is, has it attached;
one whose mailbox closes while a region still reads it goes when that
region ends. Here 40 target regions each receive from a mailbox of their
own, which then closes, while a GPU process waits, so no moment comes when
nothing runs on the device.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -fopenmp -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/region-rings-beside-process.m -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/region-rings-beside-process.m -o %t.O2
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t.O2 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
CHECK:820
CHECK-NEXT:7
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated

When main ends while the GPU process still waits, the end's check waits ten
seconds for it, and then only the process's own ring and the chunk of its
table of rings are left: the regions' rings went as each region ended.
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t.O2 leave 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LEAVE --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
LEAVE:820
LEAVE-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 1 chunks of the devices' arenas and 1 rings are allocated
